---
import BlogPost from '../../layouts/BlogPost.astro';

// Calories match each item's page on this site.
const treats = [
  { name: 'Small vanilla cone', href: '/items/vanilla-soft-serve-cone', cal: '170' },
  { name: 'DQ Sandwich', href: '/items/dq-sandwich', cal: '190' },
  { name: 'Dilly Bar', href: '/items/dilly-bar', cal: '210' },
  { name: 'Non-Dairy Dilly Bar', href: '/items/non-dairy-dilly-bar', cal: '220' },
  { name: 'Small hot fudge sundae', href: '/items/hot-fudge-sundae', cal: '~250' },
  { name: 'Strawberry sundae', href: '/items/strawberry-sundae', cal: '280' },
  { name: 'Mini Oreo Blizzard', href: '/items/oreo-blizzard', cal: '~300' },
];
const meals = [
  { name: 'Side salad (no dressing)', href: '/items/side-salad', cal: '90' },
  { name: 'Small fries', href: '/items/regular-fries', cal: '260' },
  { name: 'Grilled chicken sandwich', href: '/items/grilled-chicken-sandwich', cal: '390' },
  { name: 'Original Cheeseburger', href: '/items/original-cheeseburger', cal: '400' },
  { name: 'Cheese curds', href: '/items/cheese-curds', cal: '470' },
  { name: 'FlameThrower Stackburger', href: '/items/flamethrower-stackburger', cal: '780' },
  { name: '4-piece Chicken Strip Basket', href: '/items/chicken-strip-basket-4pc', cal: '~1,000' },
];

const faqs = [
  { q: 'What is the lowest-calorie item at Dairy Queen?', a: 'A side salad without dressing (about 90 calories) is the lightest food item. For dessert, a small vanilla cone (about 170 calories) or a DQ Sandwich (about 190 calories) are the lightest treats.' },
  { q: 'What is the healthiest thing to eat at Dairy Queen?', a: 'The grilled chicken sandwich (about 390 calories) with a side salad is one of the most balanced meals. For dessert, choose a small cone or a Mini Blizzard instead of a larger size.' },
  { q: 'How many calories are in a Blizzard?', a: 'Most Blizzards have about 300–400 calories as a Mini, 420–600 as a Small, 600–850 as a Medium and 900–1,200 as a Large, depending on the flavor.' },
  { q: 'Where can I find official Dairy Queen nutrition information?', a: 'Dairy Queen publishes nutrition and allergen details on its website and in the DQ app. Our figures are estimates to help you compare; check DQ’s information if you need exact numbers.' },
];
---
<BlogPost
  title="Dairy Queen Calories & Nutrition Guide (2026)"
  description="Dairy Queen calories at a glance: the lightest treats and meals, Blizzard calories by size, and simple swaps to eat lighter at DQ."
  h1="Dairy Queen Calories and Nutrition: Lighter Choices at DQ"
  crumb="DQ Calories Guide"
  eyebrow="Calories and nutrition"
  image="/Images/dilly-bar.webp"
  imageAlt="Dairy Queen Dilly Bar on a stick"
  datePublished="2026-04-20"
  faqs={faqs}
>
  <p class="lead"><strong>The lightest treats at Dairy Queen are a small vanilla cone (about 170 calories), a DQ Sandwich (about 190) and a Dilly Bar (about 210).</strong> For a meal, a grilled chicken sandwich (about 390 calories) or an Original Cheeseburger (about 400) are the lighter choices. The biggest calorie jump at DQ comes from size: a Large Blizzard can have three times the calories of a Mini.</p>

  <p>This guide is for comparing options. It is not medical advice, and figures are estimates that can vary by location and recipe. Check Dairy Queen’s own nutrition information if you need exact numbers.</p>

  <h2 id="treats">Lowest-calorie DQ treats</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="size-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Treat</th><th>Calories</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>{treats.map((t) => <tr><td><a href={t.href}>{t.name}</a></td><td>{t.cal}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>Treats on a stick or in a wrapper, like the Dilly Bar and DQ Sandwich, are easy to keep in check because the portion is fixed.</p>

  <h2 id="blizzards">Blizzard calories by size</h2>
  <p>Size matters more than flavor. A Mini <a href="/items/oreo-blizzard">Oreo Blizzard</a> is about 300 calories, a Small 420, a Medium 590 and a Large 920. Richer flavors like <a href="/items/reeses-blizzard">Reese’s</a> and <a href="/items/cookie-dough-blizzard">Cookie Dough</a> run higher. If you want a Blizzard but are watching calories, order a Mini. Full numbers for every flavor are on the <a href="/categories/blizzard-treats">Blizzard menu</a>.</p>

  <h2 id="meals">Calories in DQ food</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="size-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Calories</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>{meals.map((m) => <tr><td><a href={m.href}>{m.name}</a></td><td>{m.cal}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="swaps">Easy swaps to eat lighter</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Mini instead of Small</strong> on any Blizzard saves roughly 100–250 calories.</li>
    <li><strong>Side salad instead of fries</strong> saves about 170 calories (before dressing).</li>
    <li><strong>Single instead of double</strong> on a burger. The single FlameThrower is about 780 calories; the double is over 1,000.</li>
    <li><strong>Grilled instead of crispy</strong> chicken sandwich.</li>
    <li><strong>Strawberry or a cone instead of a shake.</strong> A small <a href="/items/chocolate-shake">chocolate shake</a> is about 710 calories.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="drinks">Drinks</h2>
  <p>A small <a href="/items/misty-slush">Misty Slush</a> is about 150 calories and has no fat. Shakes and <a href="/items/moolatte">MooLattés</a> are much heavier, from about 490 calories for a small. See the <a href="/categories/drinks">drinks menu</a> for every size.</p>

  <h2 id="allergies">Food allergies</h2>
  <p>If you are avoiding gluten, nuts or dairy, read our <a href="/blog/dq-gluten-free-allergen-guide">Dairy Queen allergen guide</a> before you order.</p>
</BlogPost>
